<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Exposure points</span>
      <h2>Where PHI Exposure Happens</h2>
      <p>Patient information moves through far more places than the EHR. Each one needs a safeguard and someone responsible for it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("record") }}<h3>Email</h3><p>Messages and attachments sent to the wrong recipient or a personal account.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("network") }}<h3>Shared folders &amp; cloud</h3><p>Links shared too widely and folders that never get closed.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("lock") }}<h3>EHR &amp; patient portal</h3><p>Access beyond what a role needs, and accounts not removed on departure.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("surgical") }}<h3>Personal &amp; mobile devices</h3><p>Phones and laptops with PHI and no management or encryption.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("people") }}<h3>Text &amp; chat tools</h3><p>Consumer messaging apps used for patient coordination.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("practice") }}<h3>Remote access</h3><p>Home networks and remote sessions without consistent controls.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("vendor") }}<h3>Third-party vendors</h3><p>Vendors with access to PHI and no current agreement or review.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-cell">{{ icon("policy") }}<h3>Printed records &amp; disposal</h3><p>Paper left at printers, misfiled charts, and improper disposal.</p></div>
